    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>One of the heaviest coursers outside Bretonnia, the grey-to-black Willenfelder is a powerhouse of thick muscle and sleek lines. Surprisingly fast for its bulk, the breed is relatively recent, bred by the Willenfeld stables in the County of Bocks in southern Averland. Known for a terrible temper mixed with a surprising calm in battle, the Willenfelder, when trained properly, has become the first pick for many of the more belligerent horse lords in the south of the Empire. Most are 16 hands or taller.</p>"
